29ow|a|Not long born; still in the first part of life; not yet arrived at adolescence, maturity, or age; not old; juvenile; -- said of animals; as, a young child; a young man; a young fawn. ; Being in the first part, pr period, of growth; as, a young plant; a young tree. ; Having little experience; inexperienced; unpracticed; ignorant; weak.	j:hu2,87,7;udm,74,3;2121,74,2;14xm,72,8;14x9,68,3;371,68,2;878,67,3;4xw,67,2;2931,65,12;8uz,64,13;130u,62,6;292z,61,2;c7y,60,27;18vi,59,15;htz,58,7~1hgk,18,79;c7y,60,27;17s5,24,19;18vi,59,15;1psq,42,15;1hwv,18,15;18x,54,14;1yhg,14,14;293f,53,14;c7i,38,14;8uz,64,13;2931,65,12;1m3,35,11;1xh8,24,11;1luo,16,9	e:ek,34,1;1p8k,26,16;qw7,17,11;qod,10,6;1b15,3,4~1p8k,26,16;qw7,17,11;qod,10,6;1b15,3,4;ek,34,1
