29pb|n|of Youth ; The quality or state of being young; youthfulness; juvenility. ; The part of life that succeeds to childhood; the period of existence preceding maturity or age; the whole early part of life, from childhood, or, sometimes, from infancy, to manhood. ; A young person; especially, a young man. ; Young persons, collectively.	a:pj0,100,3;fwo,68,2;13n1,63,3;16lz,36,4~16lz,36,4;pj0,100,3;13n1,63,3;fwo,68,2	v:fwo,68,2~fwo,68,2	N:n2a,64,3;acf,54,2;1e49,52,3;vzb,40,4;7nf,37,5;1b3k,37,1;1lwk,30,3~7nf,37,5;vzb,40,4;1e49,52,3;n2a,64,3;1lwk,30,3;acf,54,2;1b3k,37,1
